      "writtenOn": "2020-04-06T22:07:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How standard is it to have a \"plugdev\" group?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 1,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "24ab61caa522938e3b254c2e703b304c28e82c75",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24855309_4b9b2683",
        "filename": "extra/i2c_pseudo/50-i2c-pseudo.rules",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002022
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-06T22:30:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s still standard on Debian-based distros, but not created by default on Gentoo or Arch, it seems.  I\u0027m not sure if any group has replaced plugdev as the common way of providing access to these sorts of devices; AFAIKT the group just gets created as necessary on platforms where it doesn\u0027t exist by default.\n\nvapier@ probably has an opinion, but we could (1) not install the udev rule if plugdev doesn\u0027t exist, (2) create plugdev as a system group if it doesn\u0027t exist, or (3) install the udev rule anyway and let it fail",
      "parentUuid": "c4d26c26_a0e8a59c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 1,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "24ab61caa522938e3b254c2e703b304c28e82c75",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "12958b3e_103ca823",
        "filename": "extra/i2c_pseudo/50-i2c-pseudo.rules",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291807
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-07T01:08:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I strongly prefer avoiding (3).\n\nI\u0027m inclined to do (1) for now as the simplest alternative option.\n\nIt would be pretty neat if the install script were to offer these options interactively, or as command line flags:\n[A] Do not install udev rule.\n[B] Install udev rule using existing group.  User selects the group.\n[C] Create new group and install udev rule using it.  User names the new group.\n\n...But honestly, it\u0027s not worth the complexity.  So I prefer (1).\n\nThe real solution is of course for me to finally send this upstream.  Soon...very soon.",
      "parentUuid": "24855309_4b9b2683",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 1,
        "endChar": 57
      },
